#: manual/tutorial/score.md:92
msgid "The base score is a sum of one term per signal, and the release multiplier scales the whole sum. Scoring each signal on its own therefore splits a score into its parts:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/score.md:111
msgid "The parts add up to the total up to rounding in the last digit, which is why the check uses a tolerance instead of `==`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/score.md:114
