#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:100
msgid "Understand the order of results"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:102
msgid "Without an explicit sort, the static site orders results by how many terms of the query a package matches, then by score, then by name. The following MoonBit program reproduces this for an `OR` of words:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:154
msgid "The query `json OR parser` gives the same order on the static site: `alice/json` matches both words, and the other two tie on one match and are ordered by score. For `json AND parser` every result matches both words, so the order is the plain score order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:161
msgid "**Use the compiled module from JavaScript.** `moon build src/static_search --target js` writes an ES module with `runtime_version` and `normalize_text`; see the [static_search API](../api/static_search.md) for the import path. Check `runtime_version()` when your JavaScript code depends on the behaviour of a particular release."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:167
msgid "**Compare with the dynamic site.** The local server (`npm run dev`) runs the same query language against SQLite. Text terms there match word prefixes through FTS5 instead of substrings, and results without an explicit sort are ordered differently. The [design page](../design/static_search.md#agreement-with-the-dynamic-site) lists every difference."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:174
msgid "**Publish to GitHub Pages.** The `deploy-static` workflow runs the same commands on a schedule. Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH` when the site is served from a sub-path, so that the worker fetches `/<base>/data/...`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:180
msgid "**Implicit AND.** `json parser` without `AND` is a syntax error in the expression language. In the simple search field (`q`) the same text is one substring, `json parser`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:183
msgid "**Trimming.** `normalize_text` keeps spaces. A needle with a trailing space matches less than the trimmed one."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:185
msgid "**Field operators.** `score:180` means `score = 180`, not at least 180. Use `score>=180`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:187
msgid "**Labels are exact.** `rank=s` matches nothing on the static site; write `rank=S` and `momentum=Rising`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/static_search.md:189
msgid "**`NOT` does not raise relevance.** Only positive terms count, so for `NOT rank=D OR json` every package that mentions `json` ranks above the rest, by score among themselves, whatever its rank."
msgstr ""

